Why uv Changes Everything Here
Current Problem	uv Solution
RUN pip install flask — unpinned, slow, non-reproducible	pyproject.toml + uv.lock — exact versions, 10-100x faster
Layer cache invalidates on any dep change	Two-step copy pattern: deps layer cached separately from code layer
No Python version consistency enforcement	requires-python = ">=3.11" in every pyproject.toml
12 Dockerfiles all pattern differently	One canonical uv Dockerfile pattern across all services
requirements.txt = old-school, no transitive pinning	uv.lock pins every transitive dependency
Two Docker Patterns (applied per service complexity)
Pattern A — Multi-stage (3 feature services: ctf-dashboard, vulnerable-agent, email-agent)

Produces the smallest runtime image — uv binary and build cache never reach production:


# Stage 1: dependency builder
FROM ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:python3.11-bookworm-slim AS builder
WORKDIR /app
ENV UV_COMPILE_BYTECODE=1 \
    UV_LINK_MODE=copy

COPY pyproject.toml uv.lock ./
RUN uv sync --frozen --no-dev --no-install-project   # ← cached layer

COPY . .
RUN uv sync --frozen --no-dev                         # ← installs project

# Stage 2: slim runtime (no uv, no build cache)
FROM python:3.11-slim
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=builder /app/.venv /app/.venv
COPY --from=builder /app /app
ENV PATH="/app/.venv/bin:$PATH"
CMD ["python", "app.py"]
Pattern B — Single-stage (9 simpler services)

Still gets uv's speed and lockfile, without multi-stage overhead:


FROM python:3.11-slim
COPY --from=ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:latest /uv /bin/uv
WORKDIR /app
ENV UV_COMPILE_BYTECODE=1 \
    UV_LINK_MODE=copy

COPY pyproject.toml uv.lock ./
RUN uv sync --frozen --no-dev --no-install-project   # ← cached layer

COPY . .
CMD ["uv", "run", "python", "app.py"]
